lationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"displayed in the music notation.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Tied-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The metronome-tied indicates the presence of a tie within a metric relationship mark. As with the tied","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"element, both the start and stop of the tie should be specified, in this case within separate metronome-note","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"elements.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Tied","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Tied"}],"title":"MXLMetronome.Note.Tied","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/tied-swift.struct","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Tied-swift.struct"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The metronome-note type defines the appearance of a note within a metric relationship mark.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"title":"MXLMetronome.Note","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note"}}}